<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Format</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript.Format</AssemblyName>
    <Description>The JavaScript profile's bytecode format: opcodes, schema, encoder, decoder and the format-version range. Format versions 1 and 2 are defined; the status ledger is the authority for what each admits.</Description>

    <!-- JS-0 declares no package. The JavaScript profile's packaging decision is JS-10's and
         the status ledger records that nothing here is packable, so ADR 0001's packable set
         stays at exactly the three core packages and rule A6 keeps counting three. -->
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

    <!-- JsNativeFrame is the structure emitted machine code and managed code share, and its
         fields are pointers to unmanaged storage. The property is here rather than nowhere so
         that the ONE declaration in this component that names a pointer type is a visible,
         reviewable line in a project file instead of an assumption. Nothing in this assembly
         dereferences one; the struct is a contract, and this is what a contract about pointers
         costs to write down. -->
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- The pivot. The executor and the lowering must agree on the bytecode and neither may
       depend on the other, so both reference this and it references no project at all - not the
       core, not the profile, not the lowering. That is what makes it a sink of this profile's
       subgraph and what keeps an execution-only composition free of a compiler.
       (Revised 2026-10-16, at SJL-7.4. It read "it references nothing at all": since then it
       references one package, below, and still no project, which is what rule N3 asserts.) -->

  <!--
    THE UNICODE AREA'S OWNER (JSD-0074; milestone SJL-7.4): the property lookups, the lexical classes,
    case folding and the properties of strings the matcher and the compiler both read, over the tables
    this assembly embeds (JsUnicodeTables.g.cs, decision SJL-D-6 (c)). JSD-0074's X5 widens rule I1's
    allow-list for this edge. The package comes from the committed feed eng/packages/ at its pin, the
    lock file records its content hash, and rule I1 holds both to the allow-list, which names this
    project.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- A restore for one runtime identifier writes its lock file under obj/, as the profile's does. -->
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Broiler.Unicode.Algorithms" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
